<article class="env-lemma" id="04J9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04J9">Lemma <span data-tag="04J9">18.22.4</span>.</a> Let $(f, f^\sharp ) : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}), \mathcal{O}')$, $s : \mathcal{F} \to f^{-1}\mathcal{G}$ be as in Lemma <a href="/tag/04J8" data-tag="04J8">18.22.3</a>. If $f$ is given by a continuous functor $u : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{G} = h_ V^\# $, $\mathcal{F} = h_ U^\# $ and $s$ comes from a morphism $c : U \to u(V)$, then the commutative diagrams of Lemma <a href="/tag/04J1" data-tag="04J1">18.20.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/04J8" data-tag="04J8">18.22.3</a> agree via the identifications of Lemma <a href="/tag/04J3" data-tag="04J3">18.21.3</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal using Lemmas <a href="/tag/04J5" data-tag="04J5">18.21.5</a> and <a href="/tag/04J7" data-tag="04J7">18.22.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>